As requested, please find below the key EIS Production Support Best Practices for consideration and inclusion in the upcoming CTO presentation.

1. API Inventory Automation

Automation of the API Inventory process to enable faster, more accurate, and efficient data extraction and reporting. This practice helps reduce manual effort, minimize errors, standardize reporting, and ensure timely availability of reliable API inventory information to the client.

2. SOP Management and Process Standardization

Maintain and regularly update Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for critical EIS production support activities. This ensures consistent execution of operational processes, effective knowledge sharing, reduced dependency on individual resources, minimized operational errors, and smooth shift handovers.

3. Daily EIS Bulletin – Holistic Operational Visibility

Publish a daily EIS Bulletin providing a consolidated view of key operational activities, system performance metrics, infrastructure changes, upgrade status, and planned activities.

The bulletin includes important indicators such as average and peak TPS, server-level deployment and upgrade updates, and upcoming production activities. This practice improves stakeholder visibility, supports proactive operational planning, and ensures effective coordination between the support team and the client.

4. Proactive Monitoring and Operational Readiness

Continuous monitoring of critical EIS components, dashboards, logs, and system health indicators to identify potential issues proactively, support timely intervention, and maintain service reliability.

These practices collectively contribute to improved operational efficiency, process standardization, service quality, and stakeholder transparency.

Kindly review the above points and consider them for inclusion in the EIS Best Practices section of the CTO presentation.

